WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.717
Food has taken enough of your attention.

2
00:00:02.947 --> 00:00:05.127
Maybe it's the argument before dinner.

3
00:00:05.128 --> 00:00:08.147
Maybe it's the plan that works until the first late meeting.

4
00:00:08.721 --> 00:00:12.939
Maybe it's waking up determined to do everything differently than reaching the end of

5
00:00:13.051 --> 00:00:16.740
the day with nothing ready, no energy left for another decision.

6
00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:19.771
I'm Connor MacIvor. The Last Addiction begins

7
00:00:19.772 --> 00:00:22.891
with my own story, and it's still going.

8
00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:26.428
but I remember back when my mom tried to lose weight in the late

9
00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:30.097
1970s. In fact, I think my mom was always trying to lose that weight,

10
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.031
I think her entire life.

11
00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:37.722
Back in the late 1970s, our households switched to low-fat foods and margarine and

12
00:00:37.723 --> 00:00:39.822
Crisco. No eggs,

13
00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:41.875
of course. We drank Coca-Cola,

14
00:00:41.876 --> 00:00:45.271
believing it was safe because it didn't contain any fat.

15
00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:48.146
And I watched her struggle. And as a young boy,

16
00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:51.336
I started gaining weight, too. I had all that,

17
00:00:51.337 --> 00:00:54.779
beautiful, wonderful, sugar-laden food to eat.

18
00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:58.810
And I carried that physical and mental weight for over 45 years.

19
00:00:59.738 --> 00:01:04.650
That history made me question the ideas that I'd carried around

20
00:01:04.962 --> 00:01:08.454
food. It also made me question an answer we hear constantly,

21
00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:11.601
you know, try harder. Well, try harder doesn't prepare dinner.

22
00:01:11.888 --> 00:01:15.557
It doesn't perfect a lunch break. And it doesn't tell you what to do

23
00:01:15.558 --> 00:01:19.107
when you're hungry, exhausted. And still answering work messages.

24
00:01:19.419 --> 00:01:21.631
A useful plan has to meet you in the moment.

25
00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:26.473
And that's why I built the NO FAME Biological Firewall Blueprint.

26
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:28.874
NO FAME stands for nuts, onions,

27
00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:31.028
fish, avocados, meat, and eggs.

28
00:01:31.472 --> 00:01:34.867
It's a memorable starting point for thinking about familiar foods.

29
00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.503
It's not a claim that six categories make a complete diet.

30
00:01:37.504 --> 00:01:40.011
Your needs, preferences, allergies,

31
00:01:40.012 --> 00:01:43.111
budget, and professional advice matter.

32
00:01:43.112 --> 00:01:46.323
Foods outside the list can belong in your life,

33
00:01:46.764 --> 00:01:50.711
But in the firewall idea, let's pause before accepting another

34
00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:53.209
rule. Does this actually help me?

35
00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:57.927
Can I use it on an ordinary day? Does it fit the care I

36
00:01:57.928 --> 00:01:58.400
need?

37
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.157
Inside the Blueprint, we turn those questions into work you can do.

38
00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:08.673
First, you choose two dependable meals and an easier backup. Something

39
00:02:08.673 --> 00:02:10.831
you can obtain, prepare, and enjoy.

40
00:02:11.222 --> 00:02:14.865
Not a menu for an imaginary version

41
00:02:14.866 --> 00:02:18.907
of yourself with limited time. Then you map one difficult situation.

42
00:02:18.908 --> 00:02:21.111
What happened? What did you need?

43
00:02:21.112 --> 00:02:25.679
What did you do next? You replace an accusation about yourself with

44
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.371
information you can actually use.

45
00:02:28.372 --> 00:02:31.797
Next, you rehearse a response. If work runs late,

46
00:02:32.122 --> 00:02:34.862
what will you do? If dinner falls through,

47
00:02:34.863 --> 00:02:39.227
what is the backup? If you need rest or company as well as food,

48
00:02:39.474 --> 00:02:41.811
how will you meet that need?

49
00:02:41.812 --> 00:02:45.586
Finally, you build a way back. An imperfect meal does not create a debt.

50
00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:48.531
You return to your usual appropriate routine.

51
00:02:48.532 --> 00:02:51.449
And adjust the conditions that made the moment difficult.

52
00:02:51.778 --> 00:02:55.251
The workbook gives you 21 days of short practice.

53
00:02:55.252 --> 00:02:57.603
21 days of observation and planning.

54
00:02:58.026 --> 00:03:01.679
Not 21 days without food. Fasting is not required.

55
00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.681
There's no target weight to hit before the last page counts.

56
00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.205
You also get a clinician conversation

57
00:03:08.206 --> 00:03:10.850
planner, and a supplement question sheet.

58
00:03:11.344 --> 00:03:14.271
These help you bring useful questions to a qualified professional.

59
00:03:14.272 --> 00:03:17.165
They don't tell you to change a medicine,

60
00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.331
take a hormone, or improvise an extended fast.

61
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.207
The Blueprint

62
00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:28.051
amounts to $37, paid once. It's a digital guide and workbook you can return to.

63
00:03:28.052 --> 00:03:31.415
The practical outcome is your own operating plan.

64
00:03:31.648 --> 00:03:34.656
Dependable meals, a backup, one rehearsed

65
00:03:34.657 --> 00:03:36.866
response, and a review date.

66
00:03:37.441 --> 00:03:40.859
If you later want the self-directed inner circle library,

67
00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.834
that's a separate optional membership at 97 bucks a month.

68
00:03:44.136 --> 00:03:46.678
It contains three modules on the fasting decision,

69
00:03:46.969 --> 00:03:49.957
the food environment, and the decisions that consume your attention.

70
00:03:50.324 --> 00:03:54.534
It is not included in the $37 purchase and it doesn't turn this into

71
00:03:54.535 --> 00:03:58.783
medical care. You don't need the membership to use the Blueprint.

72
00:03:58.784 --> 00:04:01.531
Start with the work in front of you.

73
00:04:01.532 --> 00:04:05.112
It's not a promise to cure an addiction or deliver somebody else's result.

74
00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.656
It is an invitation to make the next useful decision

75
00:04:07.657 --> 00:04:09.735
easier to repeat.

76
00:04:10.321 --> 00:04:13.771
Now read what's included below. This is the kind of help you want.

77
00:04:13.772 --> 00:04:16.829
Choose the NO FAME Blueprint,

78
00:04:17.003 --> 00:04:19.891
because something you can actually use, you build it.

79
00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:23.256
It gives you more of your attention to the way you want to live

80
00:04:23.257 --> 00:04:23.799
your life.

